{"at": 1792752631.4308197, "event": "status", "reason": "the measurable target is now quantified: on the frozen host, 92.08% of the (L1,L2) cells carry exactly ONE L3 code (the mean is 1.0969 L3 codes per cell over 3612 cells), while every level's codebook is essentially fully used (243/255/256 of 256). So the third token is determined by the cell, and the codebook is NOT the bottleneck -- the residual's structure is. A candidate that enriches the third token must move that 92.08%; the level-wise metric swap does not (its pre-check was inconclusive, and the baseline is in residual_information_baseline.json)", "status": "pending", "task": "campaign:next_family_search"}
{"at": 1792752761.5858192, "event": "status", "reason": "the next family's target is now a metric the geometry demonstrably moves: the within-cell spread over the level-3 codebook's spacing is 0.7895 for the Euclidean chain and 1.4251 for a Mobius residual chain, while the redundancy itself (the fraction of (L1,L2) cells with a single L3 code) barely moves (0.9208 -> 0.9263) because it is a property of the TRAINED codebook. Any candidate in this direction is read against the 92.08% baseline", "status": "pending", "task": "campaign:next_family_search"}
{"at": 1792753069.4264758, "event": "status", "reason": "the hyperbolic/Mobius residual chain is CLOSED ON PRIOR ART before any implementation: HRQ (arXiv 2505.12404) performs residual quantization with hyperbolic operations and adapts the residual computation, and HypRQ-VAE (arXiv 2609.03369) is a hyperbolic RQ-VAE for generative recommendation. The LESSON: the prior-art search must target the OPERATOR, not the family name", "status": "blocked_no_novel_evidence", "task": "campaign:next_family_search"}
